                <pb facs="0786" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3622: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-06T18:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 7—11:58
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>622. Polish Government has expressed willingness to discuss with Soviets
                    delegation, Riga, exchange Americans in Soviet Russia. Young has informally
                    furnished list of names and suggests I ask Department as to how far matter
                    should be pressed. Request instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
